# CODEOWNERS — routes reviews; the approving-review COUNT is enforced by
# branch protection / rulesets (see CONTRIBUTING.md, risk classes).
# CODEOWNERS alone cannot require N approvers — do not rely on it for that.

# Default: general counsel owns the legal record
*                                       @journeyoflife-org/general-counsel

# Executed instruments and all marketplace legal texts — GC required (§3)
/legal-texts/                           @journeyoflife-org/general-counsel
/contracts/                             @journeyoflife-org/general-counsel

# Privileged paths — GC + retained counsel; restricted by design
/disputes/                              @journeyoflife-org/general-counsel @journeyoflife-org/retained-counsel
/regulatory/inquiries/                  @journeyoflife-org/general-counsel @journeyoflife-org/retained-counsel
/opinions/                              @journeyoflife-org/general-counsel

# Corporate records and signing authority
/corporate/                             @journeyoflife-org/general-counsel
/docs/signing-authority-matrix.md       @journeyoflife-org/general-counsel

# Employment contracts — access-restricted path
/contracts/employment/                  @journeyoflife-org/general-counsel

# Automation touching the legal record needs security in the loop
/.github/workflows/                     @journeyoflife-org/general-counsel @journeyoflife-org/security
/scripts/                               @journeyoflife-org/general-counsel @journeyoflife-org/security

# Compliance evidence linkage (lawful-basis registry cross-check)
/scripts/cross-check-consent.py         @journeyoflife-org/general-counsel @journeyoflife-org/compliance
